<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sujanpur Tira</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tira Sujanpur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sujanpur Tira is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beas">Beas</a> river in the Hamirpur district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himachal-pradesh">Himachal Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Raja Sansar Chand of Kangra made it his court in the late 18th century, building a palace and temples with wall paintings, and it became a centre of the Kangra school of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-miniature">miniature painting</a>. It is known for its large parade ground and Holi fair.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sujanpur-tira.jpg" alt="Sujanpur Tira" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Timothy Gonsalves · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tira_Sujanpur_from_Katoch_Palace_Mar19_R16_00198.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
